Z||000000||CoolBlue87GT||11-15-2001||10:17 AM||||Cliff, <P>I was wondering, what does the server, or computer we use for the forum everyday looks like.<P>Where is it located ?  Tell us some 'stuff'  about it !<P>How big is it ? / cost, etc...<p>[This message has been edited by CoolBlue87GT (edited 11-15-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||Cliff Pennock||11-15-2001||11:10 AM||||You're not far off. It's actually a black box, or a 19" rack mount computer to be more precise. It's located about 20 minutes from where I live. It lives together with a few hundred brother and sister servers (not mine of course) in a special bunker.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>It's located in a room like this one:<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/serverroom.gif"> <P>The costs? Well... I'd rather not go into that.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||CoolBlue87GT||11-15-2001||11:40 AM||||Wow, neat.  Looks like a 'clean room'.<P>A few more questions, hope you don't mind.<P>If I may ask, how / when did you start this forum ?<P>Do you have an idea on how many people are using the forum ? <P>Do you need to monitor it daily ? - (the computer, not us)<P>How much time would you guess you spend on the forum ?  - don't want to say<BR>how long I do.<P>What's it's capacities ?  Are we near out growing it ?<P>Any other things you can say about it ?<P><p>[This message has been edited by CoolBlue87GT (edited 11-15-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000003||87FieroGTx||11-15-2001||11:45 AM|||| Is the price high?(I bet it is) If so would you consider donations from forum members?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cliff Pennock||11-15-2001||12:25 PM||||&gt; <I>If I may ask, how / when did you start this forum ?</I><P>January 13, 1999. I was a member of one of the email-lists out there but I was more than unhappy with receiving so much junk in my mailbox everyday. And since I had the server I thought it would be cool to start my own forum.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>&gt; <I>Do you have an idea on how many people are using the forum ?</I><P>Not really, but my guess is between 500-5000 unique visitors each day. The forum generates about 300-500 Gigabyte of traffic each month.<P>&gt; <I>Do you need to monitor it daily ? - (the computer, not us)</I><P>Yes, I spend anywhere between 1-4 hours every day to make sure everything runs as it's supposed to run.<P>&gt; <I>How much time would you guess you spend on the forum ?</I><P>About 1-2 hours per day reading messages and another 1-2 hours maintenance.<P>&gt; <I>What's it's capacities ?  Are we near out growing it ?</I><P>It has a 100Mbit line to the backbone. The forum itself takes up about 2.1 Gigabyte of disk space and there's still more than enough space left. Since the start 17,000 images were uploaded to my server and they are still on the server. This makes it the largest collection of Fiero related images of the world.<P>It's not the physical space I'm worried about, but the traffic it generates since that is by far the most expensive. Fortunately I have a very good deal with the provider so there's no need for banners just yet.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><I>Any other things you can say about it ?</I><P>That I'm soooooo glad it runs Linux! I never have to worry about a crashing server.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I also never expected it to grow the way it did. But I'm glad there's a place where anybody can find all the information they want on Fieros. When I had my first Fiero, it was near impossible to find some information for it. That's the reason why I haven't deleted a single message yet and all messages posted here can be found in the Archives.||||reg||1
Z||000005||conductor||11-15-2001||01:45 PM||||Hulde Cliff, proud you live in our small country, famous for cheese, tulips,wooden shoes, Jan Akkerman, Adrian Vandenberg,windmills and our own Fiero: DAF?<BR>||||reg||10
